      "interactionType": "therapeutic-duplication",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "evidence": "established",
      "suggestedAction": "Use one, with the same nocturnal-breakthrough caveat as above.",
      "note": "Overlapping acid suppression."
    },
    {
      "interactingDrug": "colestipol",
      "interactionType": "pk-absorption",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "evidence": "established",
      "suggestedAction": "Separate the doses: at least 1 hour before, or 4 hours after, colestipol.",
      "note": "An anion-exchange resin binds anionic and other drugs non-selectively in the gut lumen, delaying or reducing absorption. Acidic drugs such as the NSAIDs bind particularly well. Solved entirely by spacing, since nothing is absorbed systemically."
    }
